# Line endings are the repo's, not the checkout's. Two files are compared byte
# for byte with what keel writes: src/surface.ts with the core's surface op
# (tests/surface.test.ts), and the golden fixtures with a recorded session. A
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf would give them CRLF in the working tree
# while the core and the generator write LF, and those tests would fail for a
# line ending alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.gif binary
*.png binary
